  <section class="section container prose">
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: August 2, 2026</em></p>

    <p>In accordance with FTC guidelines on endorsements and affiliate marketing, here's the full picture of how AIToolvise makes money.</p>

    <p>AIToolvise participates in affiliate marketing programs, including but not limited to those run by Writesonic, Surfer SEO, Jasper, NeuronWriter, Semrush, Claude (Anthropic), and Rankability.</p>

    <p>This means that when you click certain links on this site and make a purchase or sign up for a tool, I may earn a commission — at no additional cost to you. The price you pay is the same whether you use my link or go directly to the company's site.</p>

    <h2>This never influences my opinions</h2>
    <p>My reviews and ratings are based on my own hands-on testing and honest assessment. I only recommend tools I genuinely believe provide value, regardless of whether an affiliate relationship exists. A tool doesn't get a better score because it pays a higher commission, and a tool I wouldn't personally use doesn't get recommended just because it has an affiliate program.</p>

    <h2>Tools I personally use</h2>
    <p>Some of my affiliate partners — specifically Claude and Rankability — are also tools I use myself to run this site (for content drafting and on-page SEO, respectively). I used both before any affiliate relationship existed and would continue using them regardless. I mention this because I think it's more honest to be specific about which partners I have a personal, ongoing relationship with, rather than lump every affiliate link into one generic disclosure.</p>

    <h2>How to tell which links are affiliate links</h2>
    <p>Not every link on AIToolvise is an affiliate link — I also link to official tool websites, documentation, and sources that have no financial relationship with me at all. Where an affiliate relationship exists, it typically appears on links pointing to a tool's pricing or sign-up page within a review, comparison, or best-tools article. If you're ever unsure whether a specific link is an affiliate link, feel free to ask.</p>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>Affiliate commissions help cover the cost of running this site — hosting, the paid tool subscriptions I use to actually test what I review, and the time it takes to write and update content. It's what allows AIToolvise to stay free for readers without needing a paywall or intrusive ads.</p>

    <p>If you have any questions about my affiliate relationships, feel free to <a href="/contact/">contact me</a>.</p>

